course: dictionary
lesson: 9711
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Sultana is one of them: it can be a small dried fruit, or a title for the wife, mother or daughter of a sultan, who is a Muslim ruler. Context tells you which meaning the writer has in mind.
explain: «Grapes grow on a woody climbing vine that clings with curly tendrils and is pruned hard each winter; raisins and sultanas are dried grapes.» The grapes, the vine and the word dried all point to the fruit. A sultan's wife would not be pruned each winter!
explain: A capital letter can be a clue too. Sultana with a capital S is a title, a name for a woman in the courts of rulers such as the Ottoman Empire. Ask yourself: is this a food, or a person with a title?
explain: Words also change from place to place. In the USA, sultanas are usually called golden raisins. In Australia, New Zealand and the UK, a small box of sultanas is a common lunchbox snack.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A sultana is a dried, light-golden seedless grape, like a raisin but paler and sweeter.
fact: A sultana can also be the wife, mother or daughter of a sultan, a Muslim ruler.
fact: Sultanas go into scones, flapjacks, fruit cake and cereal.
fact: «Grapes, raisins and sultanas can badly damage a dog's kidneys», so keep them away from dogs.
exercise: «Grapes grow on a woody climbing vine that clings with curly tendrils and is pruned hard each winter; raisins and sultanas are dried grapes.» What are sultanas, according to this? | A type of scone | A kind of woody climbing vine | *A dried, light-golden seedless grape | A sultan's ruler
exercise: In the USA, what do people usually call sultanas? | Sultan's sweets | Dried figs | Green grapes | *Golden raisins
exercise: Lina says, «The Sultana sat by the window in the palace.» What is a Sultana in this sentence? | A type of vine | A kind of scone | A dried grape | *The wife, mother or daughter of a sultan
test: Mum adds sultanas to the mixture. Which of these foods do sultanas often go into? | Lollipops | Pickled onions | Fish sticks | *Fruit cake
test: «Grapes, raisins and sultanas can badly damage a dog's kidneys.» Why should you keep them away from a dog? | They turn a dog's fur golden | They are too sweet for dogs to lick | Their feeding bowl gets sticky | *They can badly damage a dog's kidneys
exam: «Grapes, raisins and sultanas are dried grapes.» Which meaning of sultana fits best in a sentence about a snack box at school? | *A dried, light-golden seedless grape | A ruler of a country | The wife of a sultan | A kind of vine
